<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
The iOS app's entitlements beside those of its provisioning profile
(application-identifier, the team's, get-task-allow): tools/ios_app.py signs
the app with them (port/ios/README.md, "Signing"):

- extended-virtual-addressing: the guest's 4 GB are reserved at once, at a
  multiple of 4 GB (port/android/host/host_memory_base.c), more address
  space than an app has without it.
- increased-memory-limit: the game's memory (the Xbox's 64 MB, its caches,
  the maps' tags, the textures in Metal's buffers) is more than the
  default limit of some devices.

No JIT: iOS gives apps no writable memory that can be made executable. The
guest's code is part of the signed executable, mapped where the guest's
memory needs it (port/ios/README.md, "The guest's code").
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
